window.DOCS["6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff"]={"id":"6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff","summary":{"title_zh":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（第三版）：全球檢視昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要執行進度","what":"這是第一工作小組的非正式文本（議程項目 9(a)，第三版），為大會第十七次會議全球檢視的決議草案。內容根據全球報告整理各國執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》的進展與缺口，並提出加速執行的「葉里溫途徑」及後續工作；方括號內為尚未同意的文字。","points":["歡迎全球報告，並注意到其主要訊息；同時歡迎締約方在綱要全部 23 個目標上都有執行的實例（第 1、3 段）。","注意到若集體執行不迅速加速，2030 年目標與使命將無法達成，因此必須處理執行上的缺口、挑戰與障礙（第 6 段）。","敦促締約方加速執行綱要（第 15 段）。","敦促尚未完成的締約方盡快完成並提交更新後的國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及第七次國家報告（第 20 段）。","敦促締約方加強國家監測與知識管理系統，以補足資料與資訊缺口（第 38 段）。","請執行秘書讓全球報告的主要發現容易取得，包括在資訊交換機制上建立資訊儀表板，並視資源情況於第十八次大會前向執行附屬機構提交相關資訊摘要（第 49 段）。"],"open":["第 7 段（整段在方括號內）：若 2030 年目標未達成，2050 年目標與願景是否可能受影響，並是否以加快提供執行手段為條件。","第 8 段：本決議與全球報告是「可」、「應」還是「將」用來指導 2026–2030 年的工作，以及採用「決定」或「同意」的用語。","第 15–16 段：加速執行的段落是否列入「單邊與脅迫性貿易措施」等執行障礙，以及是否強調全球經濟與金融體系的轉型。","第 25.bis 段：是否要求締約方減少或逐步取消有害補貼，以及是否要求已開發國家大幅提高對開發中國家的國際資源（包括官方發展援助）。","第 26 段：已開發國家增加支持的用語，例如是否加上「強烈」，以及支持是「新的」還是「新的且額外的」。","第 45 段：締約方參與區域與次區域對話的要求程度，另有一個替代條文（45 Alt）只作一般邀請。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 9 (a)"},{"t":"Planning, monitoring, reporting and review: global"},{"t":"review of collective progress in the implementation of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"Working Group I"},{"t":"Global review of collective progress in the implementation of the"},{"t":"Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework at the seventeenth"},{"t":"meeting of the Conference of the Parties"},{"t":"Non-paper"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling that, in its decisions 15/4 and 15/6 of 19 December 2022, and 16/32 of 27 February 2025, the Conference of the Parties decided to conduct a global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 1 at its seventeenth meeting and that the national reports and the global report on collective progress in the implementation of the Framework would be the primary sources of information for the global review, Recalling also that, in its decision 16/32, the Conference of the Parties also decided that the global review would draw upon relevant recommendations of the subsidiary bodies and working groups and, as relevant, the outcomes of the informal technical dialogue, [which has since been named the Kunming dialogue on collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework in support of the global review,] the outcomes of the subregional and regional dialogues on national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national reports, and the global analysis of information in national biodiversity strategies and action plans, Recognizing that 129 Parties had submitted national reports in time for consideration in the preparation of the global report, that is, by 8 March 2026, which had provided substantial evidence for preparing the global report,"},{"t":"Recognizing also that additional sources of information identified in decision 16/32, such as scientific literature and the deliverables of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services, were used in the preparation of the global report, that those sources further strengthened the evidence base for the global report and that science played an important role in the global review,"},{"t":"Noting with concern that there remain data and information gaps in the national reports, that not all Parties were able to submit national reports in time for them to be considered in the preparation of the global report and that, consequently, the experiences of some Parties, in particular small island developing States, are not well reflected in the global report,"},{"t":"Noting with appreciation the support provided to Parties for developing national biodiversity strategies and actions plans and national reports,"},{"t":"Highlighting that, for many developing country Parties, in particular small island developing States, there continues to be delays in the initiation of the Global Environment Facility support for developing national biodiversity strategies and actions plans and national reports, which had an impact on the timeliness and completeness of some national reports,2 and recognizing that a range of factors may have contributed to delays,"},{"t":"Recognizing that the information and data gaps identified in the global report do not necessarily represent gaps in the implementation of the Framework or a lack of commitment to the Framework,"},{"t":"1 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"2"},{"t":"The timing of disbursement and expenditure for the enabling activities projects funded by the Global Environment Facility is available in document CBD/SBI/7/INF/17 and summarized in the global report."}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 9 (a)\n規劃、監測、報告與審查：針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展進行全球審查\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 9 (a)<br />\n規劃、監測、報告與審查：針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展進行全球審查<br />\n第一工作小組</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"於第十七次締約方大會針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展進行全球審查\n非正式文件","html":"<p>於第十七次締約方大會針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展進行全球審查<br />\n非正式文件</p>","en":[5,6,7,8]},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"**回顧**其於 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 與 15/6，以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/32，決定於其第十七次會議進行針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展之全球審查$^1$，且國家報告與關於實施綱要集體進展之全球報告將作為全球審查之主要資訊來源，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其於 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/4 與 15/6，以及 2025 年 2 月 27 日之決議 16/32，決定於其第十七次會議進行針對實施《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之集體進展之全球審查<sup>1</sup>，且國家報告與關於實施綱要集體進展之全球報告將作為全球審查之主要資訊來源，</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"**亦回顧**其於決議 16/32 中，決定全球審查應利用附屬機構與工作小組之相關建議，以及在適當情況下，利用非正式技術對話之成果，[該對話此後被命名為「支持全球審查之關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之昆明對話」]、關於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告之次區域與區域對話之成果，以及對國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫中資訊之全球分析，","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>其於決議 16/32 中，決定全球審查應利用附屬機構與工作小組之相關建議，以及在適當情況下，利用非正式技術對話之成果，[該對話此後被命名為「支持全球審查之關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之昆明對話」]、關於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告之次區域與區域對話之成果，以及對國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫中資訊之全球分析，</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"**認識到**有 129 個締約方已及時（即於 2026 年 3 月 8 日前）提交國家報告以供準備全球報告時進行審查，這為準備全球報告提供了實質證據，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>有 129 個締約方已及時（即於 2026 年 3 月 8 日前）提交國家報告以供準備全球報告時進行審查，這為準備全球報告提供了實質證據，</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"**亦認識到**決議 16/32 中所識別之額外資訊來源（例如科學文獻與生物多樣性及生態系科學－政策平台之成果）已用於準備全球報告，且該等來源進一步強化了全球報告的證據基礎，並認識到科學在全球審查中扮演了重要角色，","html":"<p><strong>亦認識到</strong>決議 16/32 中所識別之額外資訊來源（例如科學文獻與生物多樣性及生態系科學－政策平台之成果）已用於準備全球報告，且該等來源進一步強化了全球報告的證據基礎，並認識到科學在全球審查中扮演了重要角色，</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"**關切地注意到**國家報告中仍存在資料與資訊缺口，且並非所有締約方都能及時提交國家報告以供準備全球報告時進行審查，因此，部分締約方（特別是小島嶼開發中國家）的經驗未能充分反映在全球報告中，","html":"<p><strong>關切地注意到</strong>國家報告中仍存在資料與資訊缺口，且並非所有締約方都能及時提交國家報告以供準備全球報告時進行審查，因此，部分締約方（特別是小島嶼開發中國家）的經驗未能充分反映在全球報告中，</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"**讚賞地注意到**為協助締約方制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所提供的支持，","html":"<p><strong>讚賞地注意到</strong>為協助締約方制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所提供的支持，</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"**強調**對於許多開發中國家締約方，特別是小島嶼開發中國家，全球環境基金在支持制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告方面的啟動仍持續存在延遲，這影響了部分國家報告的及時性與完整性$^2$，並**認識到**一系列因素可能導致了這些延遲，","html":"<p><strong>強調</strong>對於許多開發中國家締約方，特別是小島嶼開發中國家，全球環境基金在支持制定國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告方面的啟動仍持續存在延遲，這影響了部分國家報告的及時性與完整性<sup>2</sup>，並<strong>認識到</strong>一系列因素可能導致了這些延遲，</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"**認識到**在全球報告中識別出的資訊與資料缺口，並不一定代表綱要實施上的缺口或對綱要缺乏承諾，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>在全球報告中識別出的資訊與資料缺口，並不一定代表綱要實施上的缺口或對綱要缺乏承諾，</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"---\n$^1$ 決議 15/4，附件。\n$^2$ 由全球環境基金資助之啟動活動專案，其撥款與支出的時間點可參閱文件 CBD/SBI/7/INF/17，並彙整於全球報告中。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>1</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n<sup>2</sup> 由全球環境基金資助之啟動活動專案，其撥款與支出的時間點可參閱文件 CBD/SBI/7/INF/17，並彙整於全球報告中。</p>","en":[16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p002.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"Stressing that many Parties face institutional, technical, capacity and resource challenges in preparing national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national reports, in particular in relation to the use of the headline indicators in the monitoring framework for the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,3 which contribute to the information gaps in the global report, Acknowledging that, while there were methodological, scientific, technical and data limitations and time constraints related to the preparation of the first global report, the global report is the most definitive source of information on collective progress currently available, that it was developed through a Party-led process and that it provides a [sound] basis for the global review, Acknowledging also that the planning, monitoring, reporting and review mechanisms, including future global reviews, could be further strengthened by taking into account the experiences and lessons learned in preparing the first global report and the seventh national reports, Expressing appreciation for the work of the Ad Hoc Scientific and Technical Advisory Group for the Preparation of the Global Report on Collective Progress in the Implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework in guiding the production of the first global report,"},{"t":"Acknowledging with appreciation the financial support provided by the Governments of Germany and Netherlands (Kingdom of the) and, through the China Trust Fund, the United Nations Environment Programme for the global review, as well as the financial support provided by the European Union and the Governments of Netherlands (Kingdom of the) and Switzerland and, through the China Trust Fund, the United Nations Environment Programme for the preparation of the related global report,"},{"t":"1. Welcomes [with appreciation] the global report on collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, and notes its overarching messages and key messages;"},{"t":"2. [Also welcomes][Recognizes] with appreciation that the Framework has generated unprecedented global engagement and has driven action, innovation, collaboration and learning;"},{"t":"3. Further welcomes the fact that Parties have taken actions across all 23 targets of the Framework showing successful examples of implementation for every target;"},{"t":"4. Welcomes the fact that actors other than national Governments, namely, indigenous peoples and local communities, subnational governments, cities, and other local authorities, intergovernmental organizations, other multilateral environment agreements, non-governmental organizations, women, youth, research organizations, the business and finance community and representatives of sectors related to or dependent on biodiversity have taken action to implement the Framework;4"},{"t":"5. Highlights the fact that, as indicated in the global report, the review has revealed both progress and gaps in implementation, in particular:"},{"t":"(a) Scope and coverage"},{"t":"(i) Parties have collectively set national targets that had a higher level of scope and coverage of Targets 4, 5, 8, 9, 10 and 11 of the Framework, an intermediate level of scope and coverage of Targets 2, 3, 6, 7, 12, 13, 17 and 21 and a lower level of scope and coverage of Targets 1, 14, 15, 16, 18, 19, 20, 22 and 23;"},{"t":"(ii) The consideration of marine, coastal and inland water ecosystems, issues related to the drivers of biodiversity loss and issues related to [section C of the Framework, in particular] [whole-of-government and whole-of-society"},{"t":"3 Decision 15/5, annex I."},{"t":"4 All references to “actors other than national Governments” are to be understood as described in paragraph 4 (in line with"},{"t":"decisions 15/6 and 16/32)."},{"t":"2/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"**強調**許多締約方在編製國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及國家報告時，面臨制度、技術、能力與資源方面的挑戰，特別是關於在昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構中使用主要指標之情形，³ 這導致了全球報告中存在資訊落差；","html":"<p><strong>強調</strong>許多締約方在編製國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫以及國家報告時，面臨制度、技術、能力與資源方面的挑戰，特別是關於在昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構中使用主要指標之情形，³ 這導致了全球報告中存在資訊落差；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"**承認**雖然在編製第一份全球報告時存在方法學、科學、技術與資料的限制以及時間壓力，但該全球報告是目前可用於說明集體進展最權威的資訊來源，且該報告是透過締約方主導的程序所制定，並為全球審查提供了 [穩固] 的基礎；","html":"<p><strong>承認</strong>雖然在編製第一份全球報告時存在方法學、科學、技術與資料的限制以及時間壓力，但該全球報告是目前可用於說明集體進展最權威的資訊來源，且該報告是透過締約方主導的程序所制定，並為全球審查提供了 [穩固] 的基礎；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"**同時承認**規劃、監測、報告與審查機制（包括未來的全球審查）可以透過考量編製第一份全球報告與第七份國家報告的經驗與教訓，而得到進一步強化；","html":"<p><strong>同時承認</strong>規劃、監測、報告與審查機制（包括未來的全球審查）可以透過考量編製第一份全球報告與第七份國家報告的經驗與教訓，而得到進一步強化；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"**對**「關於編製昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要實施集體進展全球報告之特別科學與技術諮詢小組」在指導第一份全球報告製作過程中所做的努力，表示感謝；","html":"<p><strong>對</strong>「關於編製昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要實施集體進展全球報告之特別科學與技術諮詢小組」在指導第一份全球報告製作過程中所做的努力，表示感謝；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"**帶著讚賞之意承認**德國與荷蘭（荷蘭王國）政府，以及透過中國信託基金（China Trust Fund）的聯合國環境規劃署，為全球審查提供的財務支持；同時也承認歐盟、荷蘭（荷蘭王國）與瑞士政府，以及透過中國信託基金的聯合國環境規劃署，為編製相關全球報告所提供的財務支持；","html":"<p><strong>帶著讚賞之意承認</strong>德國與荷蘭（荷蘭王國）政府，以及透過中國信託基金（China Trust Fund）的聯合國環境規劃署，為全球審查提供的財務支持；同時也承認歐盟、荷蘭（荷蘭王國）與瑞士政府，以及透過中國信託基金的聯合國環境規劃署，為編製相關全球報告所提供的財務支持；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"1.\n**歡迎**[讚賞地]關於昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要實施集體進展的全球報告，並**注意到**其核心訊息與關鍵訊息；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>[讚賞地]關於昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要實施集體進展的全球報告，並<strong>注意到</strong>其核心訊息與關鍵訊息；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"2.\n[亦歡迎][承認] 綱要已激發了前所未有的全球參與，並驅動了行動、創新、協作與學習，並對此表示讚賞；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n[亦歡迎][承認] 綱要已激發了前所未有的全球參與，並驅動了行動、創新、協作與學習，並對此表示讚賞；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"3.\n**進一步歡迎**締約方已針對綱要所有 23 項目標採取行動，且每一項目標均展現了成功的實施案例；","html":"<p>3.<br />\n<strong>進一步歡迎</strong>締約方已針對綱要所有 23 項目標採取行動，且每一項目標均展現了成功的實施案例；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"4.\n**歡迎**國家政府以外的行為者，即原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協議、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性的部門代表，皆已採取行動來實施綱要；⁴","html":"<p>4.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>國家政府以外的行為者，即原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協議、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性的部門代表，皆已採取行動來實施綱要；⁴</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"5.\n**強調**如全球報告所述，審查揭示了實施過程中的進展與落差，特別是：","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>強調</strong>如全球報告所述，審查揭示了實施過程中的進展與落差，特別是：</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(a) 範圍與覆蓋範圍\n(i) 締約方集體設定的國家目標，在綱要目標 4、5、8、9、10 與 11 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面達到了較高水準；在目標 2、3、6、7、12、13、17 與 21 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面達到了中等水準；在目標 1、14、15、16、18、19、20、22 與 23 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面則達到了較低水準；","html":"<p>(a) 範圍與覆蓋範圍<br />\n(i) 締約方集體設定的國家目標，在綱要目標 4、5、8、9、10 與 11 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面達到了較高水準；在目標 2、3、6、7、12、13、17 與 21 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面達到了中等水準；在目標 1、14、15、16、18、19、20、22 與 23 的範圍與覆蓋範圍方面則達到了較低水準；</p>","en":[8,9]},{"md":"(ii) 對海洋、沿岸及內陸水域生態系、與生物多樣性流失驅動因素相關的問題，以及與 [綱要 C 節，特別是] [全政府與全社會","html":"<p>(ii) 對海洋、沿岸及內陸水域生態系、與生物多樣性流失驅動因素相關的問題，以及與 [綱要 C 節，特別是] [全政府與全社會</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"---\n³ 決議 15/5，附件 I。\n⁴ 所有提及「國家政府以外的行為者」之處，均應理解為如第 4 段所述（與決議 15/6 及 16/32 一致）。","html":"<hr />\n<p>³ 決議 15/5，附件 I。<br />\n⁴ 所有提及「國家政府以外的行為者」之處，均應理解為如第 4 段所述（與決議 15/6 及 16/32 一致）。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p003.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"approaches, including participation, the engagement of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth persons with disabilities than national Governments, gender responsiveness, equitable governance and mainstreaming], has been less addressed in national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national targets and national reports;"},{"t":"(b) (c) (d) (e) Action and implementation"},{"t":"(i) National targets associated with Targets 1, 2, 3, 8, 13, 20, 21 and 22 of the Framework were most frequently self-assessed by Parties as being on track, while national targets associated with Targets 6, 12, 15, 16, 18 and 19 were least frequently self-assessed by Parties as being on track; however, less than half of the national targets associated with any global target had been reported by Parties as being on track;"},{"t":"(ii) While there were data and national monitoring capacity gaps that limited the ability to report national data and, thus, to aggregate them at the global level and conclusively track collective progress towards the global targets, indicators related to the targets of the Framework showed negative trends more commonly than positive ones;"},{"t":"Means of implementation"},{"t":"(i) Means of implementation remain below what is required for the full and effective implementation of the Framework, especially for developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States;"},{"t":"(ii) Since the adoption of the Framework, there has been some, albeit uneven, progress across Parties in domestic and international public finance, positive incentives for biodiversity, capacity-building and development, access to and transfer of technology and technical and scientific cooperation;"},{"t":"(iii) Collectively, limited progress has been made in mobilizing and tracking private sector finance and positive incentives and in reducing incentives, including subsidies, harmful to biodiversity;"},{"t":"(iv) The lack of availability of sufficient and timely means of implementation was identified as the most common barrier to implementation, especially by developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States;"},{"t":"Whole-of-government approaches"},{"t":"(i) Parties have made progress in strengthening environmental governance, including by engaging all levels of government and all sectors; however, gaps remain with regard to policy coherence, mainstreaming biodiversity and its multiple values into national policy and engaging ministries beyond the environmental sector in implementation;"},{"t":"(ii) Gaps remain with regard to progress towards Targets 1 and 14 of the Framework, which relate to integrated planning and mainstreaming and are most directly related to whole-of-government approaches, especially in relation to integrated spatial planning, integrating biodiversity and its multiple values into policies, regulations, planning and development processes and ensuring integration across all levels of government and sectors;"},{"t":"Whole-of-society approaches"},{"t":"(i) Actors other than national Governments are actively supporting the implementation of the Framework, but indigenous peoples and local 3/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(a) 包括參與、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的參與、身心障礙者之參與（較國家政府而言）、性別回應性、公平治理及主流化]，在國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中較少被探討；","html":"<p>(a) 包括參與、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的參與、身心障礙者之參與（較國家政府而言）、性別回應性、公平治理及主流化]，在國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中較少被探討；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"(b) 行動與實施\n(i) 與《綱要》目標 1、2、3、8、13、20、21 及 22 相關之國家目標，最常被締約方自我評估為正軌進行中；而與目標 6、12、15、16、18 及 19 相關之國家目標，最少被締約方自我評估為正軌進行中；然而，與任何全球目標相關之國家目標中，由締約方報告為正軌進行中者不足半數；","html":"<p>(b) 行動與實施<br />\n(i) 與《綱要》目標 1、2、3、8、13、20、21 及 22 相關之國家目標，最常被締約方自我評估為正軌進行中；而與目標 6、12、15、16、18 及 19 相關之國家目標，最少被締約方自我評估為正軌進行中；然而，與任何全球目標相關之國家目標中，由締約方報告為正軌進行中者不足半數；</p>","en":[2,3]},{"md":"(ii) 雖然存在資料與國家監測能力之差距，限制了報告國家資料並進而於全球層級進行彙整，以及結論性地追蹤全球目標共同進度的能力，但與《綱要》目標相關之指標顯示負面趨勢的情況比正面趨勢更為普遍；","html":"<p>(ii) 雖然存在資料與國家監測能力之差距，限制了報告國家資料並進而於全球層級進行彙整，以及結論性地追蹤全球目標共同進度的能力，但與《綱要》目標相關之指標顯示負面趨勢的情況比正面趨勢更為普遍；</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"(c) 實施手段\n(i) 實施手段仍低於全面且有效實施《綱要》之需求，對於開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家而言更是如此；","html":"<p>(c) 實施手段<br />\n(i) 實施手段仍低於全面且有效實施《綱要》之需求，對於開發中締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家而言更是如此；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(ii) 自《綱要》通過以來，各締約方在國內與國際公共財政、生物多樣性之正面誘因、能力建構與發展、技術取得與轉讓，以及技術與科學合作方面，雖有進展但仍不均衡；","html":"<p>(ii) 自《綱要》通過以來，各締約方在國內與國際公共財政、生物多樣性之正面誘因、能力建構與發展、技術取得與轉讓，以及技術與科學合作方面，雖有進展但仍不均衡；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(iii) 整體而言，在動員與追蹤私部門資金與正面誘因，以及減少對生物多樣性有害之誘因（包括補貼）方面，進展有限；","html":"<p>(iii) 整體而言，在動員與追蹤私部門資金與正面誘因，以及減少對生物多樣性有害之誘因（包括補貼）方面，進展有限；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(iv) 缺乏充足且及時的實施手段，被認為是實施過程中最常見的障礙，特別是對於開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家而言；","html":"<p>(iv) 缺乏充足且及時的實施手段，被認為是實施過程中最常見的障礙，特別是對於開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家而言；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(d) 全政府方法\n(i) 締約方在強化環境治理方面已取得進展，包括參與各級政府與所有部門；然而，在政策一致性、將生物多樣性及其多重價值主流化至國家政策，以及在實施過程中參與環境部門以外之部會方面，仍存在差距；","html":"<p>(d) 全政府方法<br />\n(i) 締約方在強化環境治理方面已取得進展，包括參與各級政府與所有部門；然而，在政策一致性、將生物多樣性及其多重價值主流化至國家政策，以及在實施過程中參與環境部門以外之部會方面，仍存在差距；</p>","en":[10,11]},{"md":"(ii) 在邁向《綱要》目標 1 與目標 14 的進度方面仍存在差距，該兩項目標涉及整合規劃與主流化，且與全政府方法最直接相關，特別是關於整合性空間規劃、將生物多樣性及其多重價值整合至政策、法規、規劃與發展程序，以及確保跨所有政府層級與部門之整合方面；","html":"<p>(ii) 在邁向《綱要》目標 1 與目標 14 的進度方面仍存在差距，該兩項目標涉及整合規劃與主流化，且與全政府方法最直接相關，特別是關於整合性空間規劃、將生物多樣性及其多重價值整合至政策、法規、規劃與發展程序，以及確保跨所有政府層級與部門之整合方面；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(e) 全社會方法\n(i) 除了國家政府之外的其他行為者正積極支持《綱要》之實施，但原住民族與地方 3/11","html":"<p>(e) 全社會方法<br />\n(i) 除了國家政府之外的其他行為者正積極支持《綱要》之實施，但原住民族與地方 3/11</p>","en":[13,14]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p004.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"communities, women, youth and persons with disabilities face challenges related to limited resources, technical capacities, access to information and knowledge, effective participation and coordination mechanisms;"},{"t":"(f) (ii) Collectively, Parties have made progress in engaging actors other than national Governments in planning and implementation; however, many Parties reported challenges in accounting for the contributions of those actors in national implementation efforts;"},{"t":"(iii) While many Parties reported progress towards some elements of Targets 22 and 23 of the Framework, such as involving to a varying degree indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, persons with disabilities and other actors defined in those targets in biodiversity-related decision-making, issues related to the following were less well reflected in national targets: access to information and justice, rights over lands, territories, resources and traditional knowledge, and the protection of environmental human rights defenders or gender-responsive biodiversity governance;"},{"t":"Data and knowledge"},{"t":"(i) Parties have demonstrated improvements to national monitoring and knowledge management systems, including accounting for traditional knowledge and collecting and using information from government agencies, scientific institutions, indigenous peoples and local communities, civil society and international sources, as reflected in the progress made towards Target 21 of the Framework;"},{"t":"(ii) A total of 116 Parties reported on at least one headline indicator; the headline indicators on protected area extent (3.1), Red List Index (A.3), international public funding (D.1) and domestic public funding (D.2), which are associated with Targets 3, 4 and 19 of the Framework, were the headline indicators most reported on, while the indicators related to land-use change and land tenure in the traditional territories of indigenous peoples and local communities (22.1), benefits from the sustainable use of wild species (9.1), index of coastal eutrophication (7.1) and monetary benefits received in accordance with applicable internationally agreed access and benefit-sharing instruments (C.1), which are associated with Targets 7, 9 and 13, were the indicators least reported on;"},{"t":"(iii) For 19 of the 23 targets of the Framework, less than half of the reporting Parties submitted any data for a headline, component, complementary or national indicator; the targets with the most reported quantitative data were 1, 2, 3, 4 and 10, while Targets 8, 14, 16, 17, 20, 22 and 23 received the least;"},{"t":"(iv) The use of disaggregated indicator information, including by ecosystem type, sex, age, indigenous people and local community status or other relevant characteristics, was limited;"},{"t":"(v) Reporting against the indicators and monitoring efforts have been negatively affected by gaps, challenges and barriers related to methodologies, data availability and access, data fragmentation, technical and technological infrastructure, resource availability and capacity;"},{"t":"6. Notes with deep concern that, unless collective implementation is rapidly accelerated, including through enhanced international cooperation, improved actions and efforts and strengthened means of implementation, the 2030 targets and mission of the Framework will not be achieved, and stresses the imperative to address gaps, challenges and barriers in implementation to achieve the 2030 targets and mission;"},{"t":"4/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(f)\n社區、女性、青年及身心障礙人士面臨與資源有限、技術能力、取得資訊與知識、有效參與及協調機制相關之挑戰；","html":"<p>(f)<br />\n社區、女性、青年及身心障礙人士面臨與資源有限、技術能力、取得資訊與知識、有效參與及協調機制相關之挑戰；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"(ii)\n整體而言，締約方在讓國家政府以外之行為者參與規劃與執行方面已取得進展；然而，許多締約方報告在國家執行工作中，對於如何核算（accounting）該等行為者之貢獻面臨挑戰；","html":"<p>(ii)<br />\n整體而言，締約方在讓國家政府以外之行為者參與規劃與執行方面已取得進展；然而，許多締約方報告在國家執行工作中，對於如何核算（accounting）該等行為者之貢獻面臨挑戰；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(iii)\n雖然許多締約方報告在達成《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 22 與目標 23 之某些要素方面取得進展，例如在生物多樣性相關決策中，在不同程度上納入了原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年、身心障礙人士及該等目標所定義之其他行為者，但與下列事項相關之議題在國家目標中反映較不充分：取得資訊與司法、土地、領土、資源及傳統知識之權利，以及環境人權捍衛者之保護或具性別回應性之生物多樣性治理；","html":"<p>(iii)<br />\n雖然許多締約方報告在達成《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 22 與目標 23 之某些要素方面取得進展，例如在生物多樣性相關決策中，在不同程度上納入了原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年、身心障礙人士及該等目標所定義之其他行為者，但與下列事項相關之議題在國家目標中反映較不充分：取得資訊與司法、土地、領土、資源及傳統知識之權利，以及環境人權捍衛者之保護或具性別回應性之生物多樣性治理；</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"5.\n資料與知識\n(i)\n締約方已展現出國家監測與知識管理系統之改善，包括將傳統知識納入核算，以及收集並使用來自政府機構、科學機構、原住民族與地方社區、公民社會及國際來源之資訊，此點反映在達成《綱要》目標 21 之進展中；","html":"<p>5.<br />\n資料與知識<br />\n(i)<br />\n締約方已展現出國家監測與知識管理系統之改善，包括將傳統知識納入核算，以及收集並使用來自政府機構、科學機構、原住民族與地方社區、公民社會及國際來源之資訊，此點反映在達成《綱要》目標 21 之進展中；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(ii)\n共有 116 個締約方針對至少一項主要指標進行了報告；與《綱要》目標 3、4 與 19 相關之保護區範圍（3.1）、紅色名錄指數（A.3）、國際公共資金（D.1）及國內公共資金（D.2）之主要指標，為報告數量最多之主要指標；而與目標 7、9 與 13 相關之原住民族與地方社區傳統領土內之土地利用變化與土地權屬（22.1）、野生物種永續利用之效益（9.1）、海岸優養化指數（7.1）及根據適用之國際公認取得與利益分享機制所獲得之金錢效益（C.1）之指標，則為報告數量最少之指標；","html":"<p>(ii)<br />\n共有 116 個締約方針對至少一項主要指標進行了報告；與《綱要》目標 3、4 與 19 相關之保護區範圍（3.1）、紅色名錄指數（A.3）、國際公共資金（D.1）及國內公共資金（D.2）之主要指標，為報告數量最多之主要指標；而與目標 7、9 與 13 相關之原住民族與地方社區傳統領土內之土地利用變化與土地權屬（22.1）、野生物種永續利用之效益（9.1）、海岸優養化指數（7.1）及根據適用之國際公認取得與利益分享機制所獲得之金錢效益（C.1）之指標，則為報告數量最少之指標；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(iii)\n在《綱要》的 23 個目標中，有 19 個目標之報告締約方中，提交主要指標、組成指標、補充指標或國家指標之資料比例不足半數；定量資料報告數量最多之目標為 1、2、3、4 與 10，而目標 8、14、16、17、20、22 與 23 獲得之報告最少；","html":"<p>(iii)<br />\n在《綱要》的 23 個目標中，有 19 個目標之報告締約方中，提交主要指標、組成指標、補充指標或國家指標之資料比例不足半數；定量資料報告數量最多之目標為 1、2、3、4 與 10，而目標 8、14、16、17、20、22 與 23 獲得之報告最少；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(iv)\n分項指標資訊之使用，包括依據生態系類型、性別、年齡、原住民族與地方社區地位或其他相關特徵之分類，仍相當有限；","html":"<p>(iv)<br />\n分項指標資訊之使用，包括依據生態系類型、性別、年齡、原住民族與地方社區地位或其他相關特徵之分類，仍相當有限；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(v)\n針對指標之報告與監測工作，受到與方法論、資料可用性與取得、資料碎片化、技術與工藝基礎設施、資源可用性及能力相關之差距、挑戰與障礙所產生的負面影響；","html":"<p>(v)<br />\n針對指標之報告與監測工作，受到與方法論、資料可用性與取得、資料碎片化、技術與工藝基礎設施、資源可用性及能力相關之差距、挑戰與障礙所產生的負面影響；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"6.\n**深感憂慮地注意到**，除非透過加強國際合作、改善行動與努力以及強化執行手段，迅速加速集體執行，否則《綱要》之 2030 年目標與使命將無法達成，並**強調**必須解決執行過程中的差距、挑戰與障礙，以實現 2030 年目標與使命；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n<strong>深感憂慮地注意到</strong>，除非透過加強國際合作、改善行動與努力以及強化執行手段，迅速加速集體執行，否則《綱要》之 2030 年目標與使命將無法達成，並<strong>強調</strong>必須解決執行過程中的差距、挑戰與障礙，以實現 2030 年目標與使命；</p>","en":[10,11]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p005.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"[7. Also notes with deep concern that, if the 2030 targets and mission of the Framework are not achieved, [its 2050 goals and vision may be at risk [unless the provision of means of implementation are rapidly accelerated]];]"},{"t":"8. [Decides][Agrees] that the provisions of the present decision[, as well as the global report,] [may][are to][should] be used to guide and prioritize future work over the period 2026–2030 to address gaps, challenges and barriers and foster possible opportunities to enhance collective progress in implementation and means of implementation in relation to the 2030 targets and mission, for all Parties, but especially for developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, and that the provisions should be interpreted to be facilitative, non-intrusive and non-punitive;"},{"t":"[9. [Also decides][Reiterates][Recalls] that Parties [shall][should] retain flexibility with regard to developing [and implementing] national targets and associated actions, taking into account national circumstances, priorities and capabilities [and][within] the means of implementation available;]"},{"t":"10. Notes that the present decision is complemented by relevant decisions adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its seventeenth meeting and that the implementation of those decisions should be informed, as appropriate, by the present decision;"},{"t":"11. Also notes that the implementation of the Framework is supported by relevant decisions of the Conference of the Parties serving as the meetings of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety5 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization,6 and recognizes that the governing bodies of the respective Protocols may take into account, as appropriate, relevant provisions of the present decision;"},{"t":"12. Encourages Parties and invites indigenous peoples and local communities, subnational governments, cities, and other local authorities, intergovernmental organizations, other multilateral environment agreements, non-governmental organizations, women, youth, research organizations, the business and finance community and representatives of sectors related to or dependent on biodiversity to consider, as appropriate and relevant, the non-prescriptive approaches7 identified in the global report to address the gaps, challenges and barriers in the implementation of the Framework and to foster possible opportunities to enhanced collective progress in implementation, and notes that Parties may also use the policy-relevant actions described in relevant assessments of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services in that regard;"},{"t":"13. [Placeholder for the outcomes on the Kunming dialogue on collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework in support of the global review;]"},{"t":"13.co-chair.Alt (preambular) Expressing its appreciation to the government of China for hosting the Kunming dialogue on collective progress in the implementation of the KunmingMontreal Global Biodiversity Framework in support of the global review (hereinafter referred to as Kunming dialogue), with China and Canada serving as the co-chairs;"},{"t":"13.co-chair.Alt.bis.1 Welcomes the co-chair’s summary of the Kunming Dialogue as well as the report of the dialogue and notes that Parties, other Governments and relevant actors may wish to consider, as appropriate and relevant, the messages, approaches and lessons identified in the Kunming Dialogue with main messages from the dialogue being:"},{"t":"5 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"6 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"7 The non-prescriptive approaches are listed in section III of the global report (CBD/SBSTTA/28/2/Add.3). The reference will be"},{"t":"updated to a decision of the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties after adoption."},{"t":"5/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[7. 亦深切注意到，若未能達成 2030 年目標與綱要之使命，[其 2050 年目標與願景可能面臨風險 [除非實施手段之提供得以迅速加速]]；]","html":"<p>[7. 亦深切注意到，若未能達成 2030 年目標與綱要之使命，[其 2050 年目標與願景可能面臨風險 [除非實施手段之提供得以迅速加速]]；]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"8.\n[決定][同意] 本決議之規定[, 以及全球報告,] [可以][應當][應] 被用於指導並優先處理 2026–2030 年期間之未來工作，以應對差距、挑戰與障礙，並促進可能之機會，以增進所有締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）在與 2030 年目標及使命相關之執行與實施手段方面的集體進展，且該規定之解釋應為促進性的、非侵入性的且非懲罰性的；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n[決定][同意] 本決議之規定[, 以及全球報告,] [可以][應當][應] 被用於指導並優先處理 2026–2030 年期間之未來工作，以應對差距、挑戰與障礙，並促進可能之機會，以增進所有締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）在與 2030 年目標及使命相關之執行與實施手段方面的集體進展，且該規定之解釋應為促進性的、非侵入性的且非懲罰性的；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[9. [亦決定][重申][回顧] 締約方[應][應] 在制定[與執行]國家目標及相關行動時，應考量國家情況、優先事項與能力，[並][在]可用之實施手段範圍內，保持靈活性；]","html":"<p>[9. [亦決定][重申][回顧] 締約方[應][應] 在制定[與執行]國家目標及相關行動時，應考量國家情況、優先事項與能力，[並][在]可用之實施手段範圍內，保持靈活性；]</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"10. **注意到** 本決議與締約方大會於其第十七次會議所通過之相關決議互為補充，且在適當情況下，上述決議之執行應參考本決議；","html":"<p>10. <strong>注意到</strong> 本決議與締約方大會於其第十七次會議所通過之相關決議互為補充，且在適當情況下，上述決議之執行應參考本決議；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"11. **亦注意到** 綱要之執行受到卡塔赫納生物安全議定書$^5$與名古屋議定書（關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享）$^6$之締約方會議（即締約方大會）相關決議之支持，並**認可**各議定書之管理機構在適當情況下，得考量本決議之相關規定；","html":"<p>11. <strong>亦注意到</strong> 綱要之執行受到卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<sup>5</sup>與名古屋議定書（關於取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生利益之公平公正分享）<sup>6</sup>之締約方會議（即締約方大會）相關決議之支持，並<strong>認可</strong>各議定書之管理機構在適當情況下，得考量本決議之相關規定；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"12. **鼓勵** 締約方，並**邀請**原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協定、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性之部門代表，在適當且相關之情況下，考慮全球報告中所識別之非指令性方法$^7$，以應對綱要執行過程中的差距、挑戰與障礙，並促進可能之機會以增進執行方面的集體進展；並**注意到**締約方在此方面亦得使用政府間科學－政策平台關於生物多樣性與生態系服務之相關評估中所述之政策相關行動；","html":"<p>12. <strong>鼓勵</strong> 締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協定、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性之部門代表，在適當且相關之情況下，考慮全球報告中所識別之非指令性方法<sup>7</sup>，以應對綱要執行過程中的差距、挑戰與障礙，並促進可能之機會以增進執行方面的集體進展；並<strong>注意到</strong>締約方在此方面亦得使用政府間科學－政策平台關於生物多樣性與生態系服務之相關評估中所述之政策相關行動；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"13. [關於支持全球審查、旨在促進昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要執行集體進展之昆明對話成果之預留位置；]","html":"<p>13. [關於支持全球審查、旨在促進昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要執行集體進展之昆明對話成果之預留位置；]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"13.co-chair.Alt（序言部分）對中國政府主辦支持全球審查、旨在促進昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要執行集體進展之昆明對話（以下簡稱昆明對話）表示感謝，並由中國與加拿大擔任共同主席；","html":"<p>13.co-chair.Alt（序言部分）對中國政府主辦支持全球審查、旨在促進昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要執行集體進展之昆明對話（以下簡稱昆明對話）表示感謝，並由中國與加拿大擔任共同主席；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"13.co-chair.Alt.bis.1 **歡迎**共同主席對昆明對話之總結以及該對話之報告，並**注意到**締約方、其他政府及相關行為者在適當且相關之情況下，可能希望考慮昆明對話中所識別之訊息、方法與經驗，該對話之主要訊息為：","html":"<p>13.co-chair.Alt.bis.1 <strong>歡迎</strong>共同主席對昆明對話之總結以及該對話之報告，並<strong>注意到</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關行為者在適當且相關之情況下，可能希望考慮昆明對話中所識別之訊息、方法與經驗，該對話之主要訊息為：</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"---\n$^5$ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^6$ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^7$ 非指令性方法列於全球報告（CBD/SBSTTA/28/2/Add.3）第三節。該引用將在通過後更新為締約方大會第十七次會議之決議。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>5</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>6</sup> 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>7</sup> 非指令性方法列於全球報告（CBD/SBSTTA/28/2/Add.3）第三節。該引用將在通過後更新為締約方大會第十七次會議之決議。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p006.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"(a) Recognizing the need to close the implementation gaps identified in the global report and strongly encouraging enhanced implementation of the Framework, in particular the targets addressing indirect drivers of biodiversity loss;"},{"t":"(b) Emphasizing that achieving the Framework requires increased means of implementation including substantially increased investment in biodiversity from all sources and encouraging enhanced collective efforts in this regard and encourages parties to strengthen and scale up positive incentives for biodiversity and identify and eliminate, phase out or reform incentives harmful to biodiversity in accordance with national circumstances and priorities;"},{"t":"(c) Recognizing the importance of raising awareness of the value of nature and of enhancing the use of natural capital accounting, addressing conflicting priorities and aligning economic and policy incentives with the Framework;"},{"t":"(d) Enhancing cooperation and collaboration across ministries and foster a whole-of-society approach to enhance the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"(e) Highlighting the critical role of businesses, financial institutions and other economic actors in supporting the implementation of the Framework and the need for strengthening action, innovation, partnerships and investments that contribute to biodiversity conservation and sustainable use, including through more sustainable production and consumption patterns, and reflect the value of nature;"},{"t":"Yerevan pathway for accelerating the implementation"},{"t":"of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"14. Reaffirms the Parties’ commitment to the full and effective implementation of the Framework, including by taking into account the considerations in its section C, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities, to advance the three objectives of the Convention in a balanced and mutually supportive manner, including through enhanced international cooperation, improved actions and efforts and strengthened means of implementation; Accelerating action and implementation"},{"t":"15. Urges Parties to accelerate implementation of the Framework, including by [increased ambition [in][and by]] addressing the gaps, challenges and barriers related to implementation, as noted in paragraph 5 of the present decision, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities[, and [within] the means of implementation available to them] [recognizing that enhanced support for developing country Parties will allow for higher ambition in their actions] [16. Emphasizes that accelerating implementation would need to be supported through increased action to address [both] the underlying drivers of [and pressures on] biodiversity loss [[and barrier and dis-enablers to implementation, such as unilateral and coercive trade measures, which act as impediments to socioeconomic, economic and sustainable development in developing countries][and the global transformation of [financial systems and economic sectors that depend on nature and could be positive agents of change] economic [systems, aligning financial frameworks and mainstreaming biodiversity into relevant sectors as per national sovereignty and socio economic priorities] and financial systems] [improving the practices of][and economic sectors that have a [negative] impact on nature];] [mainstreaming biodiversity into policies, aligning financial flows with biodiversity objectives, including natural capital accounting, and taking actions that deliver multiple benefits including nature based solutions and ecosystems based approaches]][Emphasize that accelerating implement of the KMGBF will address the underling drivers of biodiversity loss and global transformation of economic and financial systems]"},{"t":"17. Invites actors other than national Governments to accelerate their contributions to the implementation of the Framework and support the implementation priorities and needs of Parties, as appropriate;"},{"t":"6/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(a) **認可**有必要彌補全球報告中所識別出的執行差距，並強烈**鼓勵**加強《綱要》之執行，特別是針對生物多樣性喪失之間接驅動因素的目標；\n(b) **強調**達成《綱要》需要增加執行手段，包括大幅增加來自所有來源對生物多樣性的投資，並**鼓勵**在此方面的加強集體努力，且**鼓勵**締約方根據國家情況與優先事項，強化並擴大生物多樣性的正面誘因，並識別且消除、逐步淘汰或改革對生物多樣性有害的誘因；\n(c) **認可**提高對自然價值之意識，以及加強自然資本會計之利用、解決衝突的優先事項，並使經濟與政策誘因與《綱要》保持一致的重要性；\n(d) 加強跨部會間的合作與協作，並促進全社會參與之方法，以強化《綱要》之執行；\n(e) **強調**企業、金融機構及其他經濟行為者在支持《綱要》執行中所扮演的關鍵角色，以及強化行動、創新、夥伴關係與投資之必要性，以促進生物多樣性保育與永續利用，包括透過更永續的生產與消費模式，並反映自然之價值；","html":"<p>(a) <strong>認可</strong>有必要彌補全球報告中所識別出的執行差距，並強烈<strong>鼓勵</strong>加強《綱要》之執行，特別是針對生物多樣性喪失之間接驅動因素的目標；<br />\n(b) <strong>強調</strong>達成《綱要》需要增加執行手段，包括大幅增加來自所有來源對生物多樣性的投資，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>在此方面的加強集體努力，且<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方根據國家情況與優先事項，強化並擴大生物多樣性的正面誘因，並識別且消除、逐步淘汰或改革對生物多樣性有害的誘因；<br />\n(c) <strong>認可</strong>提高對自然價值之意識，以及加強自然資本會計之利用、解決衝突的優先事項，並使經濟與政策誘因與《綱要》保持一致的重要性；<br />\n(d) 加強跨部會間的合作與協作，並促進全社會參與之方法，以強化《綱要》之執行；<br />\n(e) <strong>強調</strong>企業、金融機構及其他經濟行為者在支持《綱要》執行中所扮演的關鍵角色，以及強化行動、創新、夥伴關係與投資之必要性，以促進生物多樣性保育與永續利用，包括透過更永續的生產與消費模式，並反映自然之價值；</p>","en":[2,3,4,5]},{"md":"加速執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之葉里溫路徑","html":"<p>加速執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之葉里溫路徑</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"14. **重申**締約方對於全面且有效執行《綱要》之承諾，包括根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，並考量其 C 節之考量因素，以平衡且相互支持的方式推進公約之三大目標，包括透過加強國際合作、改善行動與努力，以及強化執行手段；","html":"<p>14. <strong>重申</strong>締約方對於全面且有效執行《綱要》之承諾，包括根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，並考量其 C 節之考量因素，以平衡且相互支持的方式推進公約之三大目標，包括透過加強國際合作、改善行動與努力，以及強化執行手段；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"加速行動與執行","html":"<p>加速行動與執行</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"15. **敦促**締約方加速執行《綱要》，包括透過 [增加雄心 [在][以及透過]] 解決本決議第 5 段所述之與執行相關的差距、挑戰與障礙，並根據國家情況、優先事項與能力[, 且 [在] 他們可用的執行手段範圍內] [認可對開發中國家締約方之加強支持，將使其行動具備更高的雄心]","html":"<p>15. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方加速執行《綱要》，包括透過 [增加雄心 [在][以及透過]] 解決本決議第 5 段所述之與執行相關的差距、挑戰與障礙，並根據國家情況、優先事項與能力[, 且 [在] 他們可用的執行手段範圍內] [認可對開發中國家締約方之加強支持，將使其行動具備更高的雄心]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"[16. **強調**加速執行需要透過增加行動來獲得支持，以應對 [同時] 生物多樣性喪失的底層驅動因素 [以及對生物多樣性的壓力] [[以及執行之障礙與阻礙因素，例如單方面且強制性的貿易措施，這些措施對開發中國家的社會經濟、經濟與永續發展構成阻礙][以及 [依賴自然且可能成為積極變革代理人的] 金融系統與經濟部門之全球轉型 經濟 [系統，根據國家主權與社會經濟優先事項，使金融框架一致化並將生物多樣性主流化至相關部門] 與金融系統] [改善][且對自然具有 [負面] 影響之經濟部門的實務]；] [將生物多樣性主流化至政策中，使金融流向與生物多樣性目標一致，包括自然資本會計，並採取能帶來多重效益的行動，包括基於自然的解決方案與基於生態系的方案]][強調加速執行 KMGBF 將應對生物多樣性喪失的底層驅動因素，以及經濟與金融系統的全球轉型]","html":"<p>[16. <strong>強調</strong>加速執行需要透過增加行動來獲得支持，以應對 [同時] 生物多樣性喪失的底層驅動因素 [以及對生物多樣性的壓力] [[以及執行之障礙與阻礙因素，例如單方面且強制性的貿易措施，這些措施對開發中國家的社會經濟、經濟與永續發展構成阻礙][以及 [依賴自然且可能成為積極變革代理人的] 金融系統與經濟部門之全球轉型 經濟 [系統，根據國家主權與社會經濟優先事項，使金融框架一致化並將生物多樣性主流化至相關部門] 與金融系統] [改善][且對自然具有 [負面] 影響之經濟部門的實務]；] [將生物多樣性主流化至政策中，使金融流向與生物多樣性目標一致，包括自然資本會計，並採取能帶來多重效益的行動，包括基於自然的解決方案與基於生態系的方案]][強調加速執行 KMGBF 將應對生物多樣性喪失的底層驅動因素，以及經濟與金融系統的全球轉型]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"17. **邀請**國家政府以外的行為者，在適當情況下，加速其對執行《綱要》之貢獻，並支持締約方的執行優先事項與需求；","html":"<p>17. <strong>邀請</strong>國家政府以外的行為者，在適當情況下，加速其對執行《綱要》之貢獻，並支持締約方的執行優先事項與需求；</p>","en":[10,11]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p007.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"18. Welcomes the voluntary coalitions, partnerships, initiatives and multi-stakeholder platforms that have been established to support the implementation of the Framework, and encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and actors other than national Governments, to make effective use of relevant existing initiatives, and, where needed, establish new ones, aimed at enhancing the implementation of the Framework, prioritizing the targets and cross-cutting elements of the Framework for where Parties have reported the least progress towards their national targets, as identified in subparagraph 5 (b), and in a manner that is supportive of implementation by Parties at the national level, noting that such initiatives may complement and contribute to means of implementation and should not be seen as a substitute for the obligations of all Parties under the Convention regarding means of implementation;"},{"t":"19. Welcomes the support provided by relevant partners, including the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres, the secretariats of multilateral environmental agreements, United Nations entities, intergovernmental organizations, nongovernmental organizations and research networks, to implement the Framework, and invites these partners to provide further support, paying particular attention to areas where progress remains insufficient, while responding to the needs and priorities identified by Parties, especially developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island development States[, and Parties with economies in transition], including by facilitating peer-to-peer learning, North-South, South-South and triangular cooperation and information exchange;"},{"t":"Enhancing scope and coverage"},{"t":"20. Urges Parties that have not yet done so to finalize and submit their revised or updated national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national targets and seventh national report as soon as possible, noting that the submission of national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national reports are obligations under Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention, and, where relevant and in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities, take into account the gaps, challenges, barriers and opportunities identified in the global report, in particular the gaps and progress identified in paragraph 5 above;"},{"t":"21. Encourages Parties who have not already done so, on a voluntary basis, to develop, through inclusive processes, national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, capacitybuilding and monitoring plans to guide effective implementation, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities;"},{"t":"22"},{"t":"Recognizes that Parties that wish to do so, and in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities, may further strengthen [the scope and coverage of] [the ambition towards] their commitments towards the implementation of the Framework through national instruments, as appropriate and where relevant, noting the gaps described in paragraph 5 above, including the consideration of marine, coastal and inland water ecosystems, while further recognizing that the extent and pace that Parties, especially developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing states, are able to do so depends on the availability of adequate, predictable, timely and easily accessible means of implementation, and while ensuring that such development or revision does not divert attention or resources away from actions to implement the Framework;"},{"t":"Strengthening means of implementation"},{"t":"23. Recognizes that the full and effective implementation of the Framework relies, inter alia, on the availability of sufficient and timely means of implementation, including financial resources, capacity, technology and technical and scientific resources, and that gaps in means of implementation are the most common barriers for the full and effective implementation of the Framework, especially for developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, as noted in paragraph 5;"},{"t":"7/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"18. **歡迎**為支持綱要實施而建立的自願性聯盟、夥伴關係、倡議及多方利害關係人平台，並**鼓勵**締約方，且**邀請**國家政府以外的其他政府與行為者，有效利用相關現有倡議，並在必要時建立新倡議，旨在強化綱要之實施，並針對第 5 (b) 小節所識別、締約方在達成其國家目標方面進展最少之目標與橫向要素，優先進行處理，且其方式應支持締約方在國家層級之實施，並**注意到**此類倡議可補充並有助於實施手段，且不應被視為取代所有締約方在公約下關於實施手段之義務；","html":"<p>18. <strong>歡迎</strong>為支持綱要實施而建立的自願性聯盟、夥伴關係、倡議及多方利害關係人平台，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，且<strong>邀請</strong>國家政府以外的其他政府與行為者，有效利用相關現有倡議，並在必要時建立新倡議，旨在強化綱要之實施，並針對第 5 (b) 小節所識別、締約方在達成其國家目標方面進展最少之目標與橫向要素，優先進行處理，且其方式應支持締約方在國家層級之實施，並<strong>注意到</strong>此類倡議可補充並有助於實施手段，且不應被視為取代所有締約方在公約下關於實施手段之義務；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"19. **歡迎**相關夥伴為實施綱要所提供的支持，包括區域與次區域技術及科學合作支持中心、多邊環境協議秘書處、聯合國實體、政府間組織、非政府組織及研究網絡，並**邀請**這些夥伴提供進一步支持，特別關注進展仍不充分之領域，同時回應締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家[, 以及經濟轉型中之締約方]）所識別之需求與優先事項，包括透過促進同儕學習、南北合作、南南合作與三角合作及資訊交換；","html":"<p>19. <strong>歡迎</strong>相關夥伴為實施綱要所提供的支持，包括區域與次區域技術及科學合作支持中心、多邊環境協議秘書處、聯合國實體、政府間組織、非政府組織及研究網絡，並<strong>邀請</strong>這些夥伴提供進一步支持，特別關注進展仍不充分之領域，同時回應締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家[, 以及經濟轉型中之締約方]）所識別之需求與優先事項，包括透過促進同儕學習、南北合作、南南合作與三角合作及資訊交換；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"強化範圍與覆蓋範圍","html":"<p>強化範圍與覆蓋範圍</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"20. **敦促**尚未完成之締約方盡快完成並提交其修訂或更新之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及第七次國家報告，並**注意到**提交國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告乃公約第六條與第二十六條下之義務，且在相關且符合國家情況、優先事項與能力之情況下，應考量全球報告中所識別之差距、挑戰、障礙與機會，特別是上述第五段所識別之差距與進展；","html":"<p>20. <strong>敦促</strong>尚未完成之締約方盡快完成並提交其修訂或更新之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及第七次國家報告，並<strong>注意到</strong>提交國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告乃公約第六條與第二十六條下之義務，且在相關且符合國家情況、優先事項與能力之情況下，應考量全球報告中所識別之差距、挑戰、障礙與機會，特別是上述第五段所識別之差距與進展；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"21. **鼓勵**尚未進行之締約方在自願基礎上，透過包容性程序，根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，制定國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具、能力建構與監測計畫，以指導有效實施；","html":"<p>21. <strong>鼓勵</strong>尚未進行之締約方在自願基礎上，透過包容性程序，根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，制定國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具、能力建構與監測計畫，以指導有效實施；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"22. **認可**欲進行之締約方，在符合國家情況、優先事項與能力之情況下，得在適當且相關之處，透過國家工具進一步強化其關於實施綱要之承諾[範圍與覆蓋範圍][對……之雄心]，並**注意到**上述第五段所述之差距，包括對海洋、沿海及內陸水域生態系之考量；同時進一步**認可**締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）能夠達成此目標之程度與步調，取決於是否具備充足、可預測、及時且易於取得之實施手段，且在確保此類發展或修訂不會將注意力或資源從實施綱要之行動中轉移出去之同時；","html":"<p>22. <strong>認可</strong>欲進行之締約方，在符合國家情況、優先事項與能力之情況下，得在適當且相關之處，透過國家工具進一步強化其關於實施綱要之承諾[範圍與覆蓋範圍][對……之雄心]，並<strong>注意到</strong>上述第五段所述之差距，包括對海洋、沿海及內陸水域生態系之考量；同時進一步<strong>認可</strong>締約方（特別是開發中締約方，尤其是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）能夠達成此目標之程度與步調，取決於是否具備充足、可預測、及時且易於取得之實施手段，且在確保此類發展或修訂不會將注意力或資源從實施綱要之行動中轉移出去之同時；</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"強化實施手段","html":"<p>強化實施手段</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"23. **認可**綱要之全面且有效實施，除其他外，仰賴於充足且及時之實施手段之可用性，包括財務資源、能力、技術以及技術與科學資源，且實施手段之差距乃全面且有效實施綱要最常見之障礙，對於開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）而言尤甚，如第五段所述；","html":"<p>23. <strong>認可</strong>綱要之全面且有效實施，除其他外，仰賴於充足且及時之實施手段之可用性，包括財務資源、能力、技術以及技術與科學資源，且實施手段之差距乃全面且有效實施綱要最常見之障礙，對於開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）而言尤甚，如第五段所述；</p>","en":[9,10]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p008.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"24. Invites Parties, on a voluntary basis and as appropriate, to identify specific priorities to implement their national biodiversity strategies and action plans and corresponding necessary means of implementation, and to reflect those needs in relevant plans and policies and share that information, where relevant and appropriate;"},{"t":"25. Encourages Parties, in accordance with national circumstances, priorities and capabilities, to mobilize domestic and international public and private finance for biodiversity in line with a view to filling the gaps identified in paragraph 5 above;"},{"t":"[25.bis"},{"t":"[Urges] Parties to [reduce [and or phase out] perverse incentives, such as"},{"t":"subsidies harmful to biodiversity, and scale up positive incentives] [accelerate identification and eliminate, phase out or reform incentives, including subsidies, harmful for biodiversity, in a proportionate, just, fair, effective and equitable way, and scale up positive incentives][in line with Target 18 of the Framework][and dramatically scale up total biodiversity related international resources from developed countries, including ODA, and from countries that voluntary assume the obligations of developing country parties to developing country parties, in particular, LDCs and SIDS and EIT] in line with a view to filling the gaps identified in paragraph 5 above;]"},{"t":"26. [Strongly] Encourages developed country Parties, and invites other Parties in a position to do so on a voluntary basis, as well as other Governments, multilateral and bilateral agencies and funds and other relevant organizations, to increase their support, including through [scaled up,][the provision of][the provision and mobilization of][new][new and additional], adequate, predictable and timely means of implementation in an easily accessible manner, such as simplified access procedures and strengthened country ownership of supported activities, and to continue to provide transparent information on the resources provided for developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States[, and Parties with economies in transition] [with the aim of addressing the persistent gaps between the needs identified by Parties and the resources provided];"},{"t":"27. Requests the Global Environment Facility to enhance the provision of adequate, predictable, timely and transparent means of implementation in an easily accessible manner to developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, including by simplifying access procedures and strengthening country ownership of activities to support the Framework, in accordance with national biodiversity strategies and action plans, and to share through existing reporting arrangements, and without creating additional burdens, detailed information on the resources provided and how they address the needs and priorities identified by Parties through their projects, without prejudice to the process established under decision[s] 16/34 of 27 February 2025 [and 17/--];"},{"t":"28. Also requests the Global Environment Facility and its implementing agencies, including the United Nations Development Programme in the context of the Biodiversity Finance Initiative, to expedite the support to all eligible Parties on their enabling support activities for the development of biodiversity finance plans, in order to unlock financial resources for the implementation of national biodiversity strategies and action plans, as described in decision 15/7 of 19 December 2022; [29. Encourages Parties and invites other Governments, multilateral and bilateral agencies and funds and other organizations to facilitate access to means of implementation for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth;]"},{"t":"30. Invites relevant organizations, including the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, to continue to provide support for strengthening capacity-building and development initiatives and addressing gaps and challenges at the national and subnational levels; Engaging the whole of government"},{"t":"31. Invites Parties, in accordance with their national circumstances and priorities, to strengthen the whole-of-government-approach to implementation, including by strengthening institutional, inter-institutional, policy, legal, fiscal, budgetary and regulatory coordination 8/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"24. **邀請**締約方在自願且適當的情況下，確定執行其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之特定優先事項及相應之必要執行手段，並在相關且適當時，將該等需求反映於相關計畫與政策中，並分享該等資訊；\n25. **鼓勵**締約方根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，為生物多樣性動員國內及國際之公共與私人資金，以期填補上述第 5 段所確定之差距；\n[25.bis\n[敦促] 締約方[減少[及或逐步淘汰]扭曲之誘因，例如對生物多樣性有害之補貼，並擴大正向誘因][加速識別並以比例、公正、公平、有效且衡平的方式，消除、逐步淘汰或改革對生物多樣性有害之誘因，包括補貼][符合綱要目標 18][並大幅擴大來自已開發國家（包括官方發展援助，ODA）以及自願承擔開發中國家締約方義務之國家，向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中國家之總體生物多樣性相關國際資源]，以期填補上述第 5 段所確定之差距；]\n26. [強烈] **鼓勵**已開發國家締約方，並**邀請**有能力且在自願基礎上之其他締約方，以及其他政府、多邊與雙邊機構及基金與其他相關組織，增加其支持，包括透過[擴大][提供][提供與動員][新][新且額外]、充足、可預測且及時之執行手段，並以易於取得之方式（例如簡化取得程序及加強受支持活動之國家自主權），並繼續針對向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家[, 以及經濟轉型中國家]提供之資源，提供透明資訊[旨在解決締約方所確定之需求與所提供資源之間持續存在之差距]；\n27. **請求**全球環境基金以易於取得之方式，加強向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中國家，提供充足、可預測、及時且透明之執行手段，包括透過簡化取得程序及加強支持綱要之活動之國家自主權，並根據國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，透過現有報告機制，在不增加額外負擔的情況下，分享關於所提供資源之詳細資訊，以及該等資源如何透過其專案解決締約方所確定之需求與優先事項，且不損害根據 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議[s] 16/34 [及 17/--] 所建立之程序；\n28. 亦**請求**全球環境基金及其執行機構，包括聯合國開發計畫在生物多樣性融資倡議背景下之角色，加速對所有符合資格締約方在開發生物多樣性融資計畫之賦能支持活動方面之支持，以釋放用於執行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之財務資源，如 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/7 所述；\n[29. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、多邊與雙邊機構及基金與其他組織，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年取得執行手段之便利性；]\n30. **邀請**相關組織，包括技術與科學合作支持中心，繼續提供支持，以加強能力建構與發展倡議，並應對國家與次國家級層面之差距與挑戰；","html":"<p>24. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方在自願且適當的情況下，確定執行其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之特定優先事項及相應之必要執行手段，並在相關且適當時，將該等需求反映於相關計畫與政策中，並分享該等資訊；<br />\n25. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方根據國家情況、優先事項與能力，為生物多樣性動員國內及國際之公共與私人資金，以期填補上述第 5 段所確定之差距；<br />\n[25.bis<br />\n[敦促] 締約方[減少[及或逐步淘汰]扭曲之誘因，例如對生物多樣性有害之補貼，並擴大正向誘因][加速識別並以比例、公正、公平、有效且衡平的方式，消除、逐步淘汰或改革對生物多樣性有害之誘因，包括補貼][符合綱要目標 18][並大幅擴大來自已開發國家（包括官方發展援助，ODA）以及自願承擔開發中國家締約方義務之國家，向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中國家之總體生物多樣性相關國際資源]，以期填補上述第 5 段所確定之差距；]<br />\n26. [強烈] <strong>鼓勵</strong>已開發國家締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>有能力且在自願基礎上之其他締約方，以及其他政府、多邊與雙邊機構及基金與其他相關組織，增加其支持，包括透過[擴大][提供][提供與動員][新][新且額外]、充足、可預測且及時之執行手段，並以易於取得之方式（例如簡化取得程序及加強受支持活動之國家自主權），並繼續針對向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家[, 以及經濟轉型中國家]提供之資源，提供透明資訊[旨在解決締約方所確定之需求與所提供資源之間持續存在之差距]；<br />\n27. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金以易於取得之方式，加強向開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型中國家，提供充足、可預測、及時且透明之執行手段，包括透過簡化取得程序及加強支持綱要之活動之國家自主權，並根據國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，透過現有報告機制，在不增加額外負擔的情況下，分享關於所提供資源之詳細資訊，以及該等資源如何透過其專案解決締約方所確定之需求與優先事項，且不損害根據 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議[s] 16/34 [及 17/--] 所建立之程序；<br />\n28. 亦<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金及其執行機構，包括聯合國開發計畫在生物多樣性融資倡議背景下之角色，加速對所有符合資格締約方在開發生物多樣性融資計畫之賦能支持活動方面之支持，以釋放用於執行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之財務資源，如 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/7 所述；<br />\n[29. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、多邊與雙邊機構及基金與其他組織，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年取得執行手段之便利性；]<br />\n30. <strong>邀請</strong>相關組織，包括技術與科學合作支持中心，繼續提供支持，以加強能力建構與發展倡議，並應對國家與次國家級層面之差距與挑戰；</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"落實全政府參與\n31. **邀請**締約方根據其國家情況與優先事項，加強執行之全政府方法，包括透過加強制度、跨制度、政策、法律、財政、預算與監管協調","html":"<p>落實全政府參與<br />\n31. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方根據其國家情況與優先事項，加強執行之全政府方法，包括透過加強制度、跨制度、政策、法律、財政、預算與監管協調</p>","en":[10]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p009.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"mechanisms, integrated planning, monitoring and reporting processes, and mainstreaming biodiversity and its multiple values across and within sectors;"},{"t":"32. Encourages Parties, in accordance with their national circumstances and priorities, to promote policy coherence across biodiversity and other areas, including climate, food, water, health, land-use and sustainable development, in, inter alia, the implementation of national strategies and policies developed under the Rio conventions and other biodiversity-related multilateral environment agreements;"},{"t":"33. Invites Parties to integrate commitments and actions in support of the implementation of the Framework from subnational and local governments and different sectors of government in their national biodiversity strategies and action plans and in their national targets and national reports, as appropriate and where relevant;"},{"t":"Engaging the whole of society"},{"t":"34. Emphasizes that actions from indigenous peoples and local communities, subnational governments, cities, and other local authorities, intergovernmental organizations, other multilateral environment agreements, non-governmental organizations, women, youth, research organizations, the business and finance community and representatives of sectors related to or dependent on biodiversity contribute to the implementation of the Framework, including through NBSAPs, and that a more effective use of their contributions, knowledge, expertise and initiatives could represent a significant opportunity to accelerate the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"35. Encourages Parties to strengthen the engagement of all actors other than national Governments, [in particular] [including] [by enabling the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive participation and engagement] of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, in order to ensure that such actors are involved in consultation processes, planning and implementation, in accordance with national legislation;"},{"t":"36. Invites actors other than national Governments to share information with Parties on their actions in relation to the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"37. Invites Parties, [in accordance with their national circumstances and priorities,] to reflect commitments and actions in support of the implementation of the Framework by actors other than national Governments, in particular from indigenous peoples and local communities, women, and youth, in their national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national targets and national reports, as appropriate and where relevant;"},{"t":"Enhancing monitoring and knowledge"},{"t":"38. Urges Parties to further develop and/or strengthen national monitoring and knowledge management systems to address the gaps in data and knowledge mentioned above and to improve evidenced-based decision-making and the tracking of national progress in the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"[39. Encourages Parties to ensure that the foundational data needed for implementing the monitoring framework, in particular national ecosystem maps, are in place to support the operationalization of the ecosystem-based headline indicators;]"},{"t":"[40. Also encourages Parties, and [requests][invites] the Global Environment Facility and invites other Governments and other organizations, to provide support for addressing the technical and financial challenges faced by Parties, especially developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, in improving their national monitoring and knowledge management systems [and foundational data needed for implementing and monitoring the Framework], including by enhancing the provision of adequate, predictable, accessible and timely financial resources, technology transfer [on favourable terms, including on concessional and preferential terms, as mutually agreed][on mutually agreed terms], technical assistance and capacitybuilding and development to developing country Parties in order to enable the effective 9/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 版本 3 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"機制、整合性規劃、監測與報告流程，以及在各部門之間及部門內部將生物多樣性及其多元價值進行主流化；","html":"<p>機制、整合性規劃、監測與報告流程，以及在各部門之間及部門內部將生物多樣性及其多元價值進行主流化；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"32. **鼓勵**締約方根據其國情與優先事項，在執行根據里約公約（Rio conventions）及其他與生物多樣性相關之多邊環境協議所制定之國家策略與政策時，於其他方面促進生物多樣性與其他領域（包括氣候、糧食、水、健康、土地利用及永續發展）之間的政策一致性；","html":"<p>32. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方根據其國情與優先事項，在執行根據里約公約（Rio conventions）及其他與生物多樣性相關之多邊環境協議所制定之國家策略與政策時，於其他方面促進生物多樣性與其他領域（包括氣候、糧食、水、健康、土地利用及永續發展）之間的政策一致性；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"33. **邀請**締約方在適當且相關之情況下，將來自次國家級政府、地方政府及政府不同部門支持執行《綱要》之承諾與行動，納入其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中；","html":"<p>33. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方在適當且相關之情況下，將來自次國家級政府、地方政府及政府不同部門支持執行《綱要》之承諾與行動，納入其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"**動員全社會**","html":"<p><strong>動員全社會</strong></p>","en":[4]},{"md":"34. **強調**原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協議、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性之部門代表，其所採取之行動（包括透過國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫）皆有助於《綱要》之執行；且更有效地利用其貢獻、知識、專業技術與倡議，可望成為加速執行《綱要》之重大契機；","html":"<p>34. <strong>強調</strong>原住民族與地方社區、次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局、政府間組織、其他多邊環境協議、非政府組織、女性、青年、研究機構、企業與金融界，以及與生物多樣性相關或依賴生物多樣性之部門代表，其所採取之行動（包括透過國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫）皆有助於《綱要》之執行；且更有效地利用其貢獻、知識、專業技術與倡議，可望成為加速執行《綱要》之重大契機；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"35. **鼓勵**締約方加強國家政府以外所有行為者的參與，[特別是] [包括] [透過確保原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之充分、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之參與及投入]，以確保該等行為者能根據國家立法，參與諮詢、規劃與執行程序；","html":"<p>35. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方加強國家政府以外所有行為者的參與，[特別是] [包括] [透過確保原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之充分、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應之參與及投入]，以確保該等行為者能根據國家立法，參與諮詢、規劃與執行程序；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"36. **邀請**國家政府以外之行為者，與締約方分享其關於執行《綱要》之行動資訊；","html":"<p>36. <strong>邀請</strong>國家政府以外之行為者，與締約方分享其關於執行《綱要》之行動資訊；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"37. **邀請**締約方，[根據其國情與優先事項，] 在適當且相關之情況下，於其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中，反映國家政府以外之行為者（特別是原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年）支持執行《綱要》之承諾與行動；","html":"<p>37. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方，[根據其國情與優先事項，] 在適當且相關之情況下，於其國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中，反映國家政府以外之行為者（特別是原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年）支持執行《綱要》之承諾與行動；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"**強化監測與知識**","html":"<p><strong>強化監測與知識</strong></p>","en":[9]},{"md":"38. **敦促**締約方進一步開發及／或強化國家監測與知識管理系統，以解決上述資料與知識之差距，並改善以證據為基礎之決策，以及追蹤執行《綱要》之國家進度；","html":"<p>38. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方進一步開發及／或強化國家監測與知識管理系統，以解決上述資料與知識之差距，並改善以證據為基礎之決策，以及追蹤執行《綱要》之國家進度；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"[39. **鼓勵**締約方確保執行監測架構所需之基礎資料（特別是國家生態系地圖）已到位，以支持以生態系為基礎之主要指標之運作；]","html":"<p>[39. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方確保執行監測架構所需之基礎資料（特別是國家生態系地圖）已到位，以支持以生態系為基礎之主要指標之運作；]</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"[40. 亦**鼓勵**締約方，並[請求][邀請]全球環境基金，且**邀請**其他政府及其他組織，為解決締約方（特別是開發中國家締約方，尤其是低度開發國家及小島嶼開發中國家）在改善其國家監測與知識管理系統[以及執行與監測《綱要》所需之基礎資料]方面所面臨之技術與財務挑戰提供支持，包括透過強化提供充足、可預測、可取得且及時之財務資源、技術轉移[以優惠條件，包括依共同商定之優惠與特惠條件][依共同商定之條件]、技術援助與能力建構及發展，以向開發中國家締約方提供，旨在實現有效之","html":"<p>[40. 亦<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並[請求][邀請]全球環境基金，且<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府及其他組織，為解決締約方（特別是開發中國家締約方，尤其是低度開發國家及小島嶼開發中國家）在改善其國家監測與知識管理系統[以及執行與監測《綱要》所需之基礎資料]方面所面臨之技術與財務挑戰提供支持，包括透過強化提供充足、可預測、可取得且及時之財務資源、技術轉移[以優惠條件，包括依共同商定之優惠與特惠條件][依共同商定之條件]、技術援助與能力建構及發展，以向開發中國家締約方提供，旨在實現有效之</p>","en":[12]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p010.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"implementation of the monitoring framework and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;8]"},{"t":"41. Invites actors other than national Governments, the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, the secretariats of biodiversity-related conventions and other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, United Nations entities and intergovernmental organizations to support the efforts of Parties to improve national monitoring and knowledge management systems;"},{"t":"42. Encourages Parties to make full use of existing mechanisms, tools, the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, capacity-building and development initiatives and plans, and enhanced regional cooperation to strengthen monitoring and knowledge management systems;"},{"t":"43. Invites Parties, other Governments, actors other than national Governments and the technical and scientific cooperation support centres supporting the implementation of the Framework to make use of the information that is contained in the global report and the national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national targets and national reports, when executing their respective mandates, and that is within their area of competence, where relevant;"},{"t":"44. Encourages Parties and actors other than national Governments to share experiences, lessons learned and best practices in the implementation of the Framework, including by uploading them to the virtual library of the clearing-house mechanism, and invites Parties to make use of that information, where relevant;"},{"t":"[45. Invites Parties to engage in regional and subregional dialogues on the global review and the Yerevan Pathway for accelerating implementation of the Framework[[, in line with paragraph 20 of decision 15/6] [, with a view to sharing actions and efforts, as appropriate][and share [any][their] respective actions and efforts, as appropriate;]]]"},{"t":"[45. Alt"},{"t":"Invites Parties to engage in regional and subregional dialogues for accelerating the implementation of the Framework;]"},{"t":"46. Invites relevant partner organizations, in particular, the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, in coordination with the Secretariat, to conduct workshops or dialogues, building on existing processes, as appropriate, on the findings of the first global review, with a view to promoting peer-to-peer learning and sharing experiences and best practices;"},{"t":"47. Invites the United Nations Environment Programme to organize a fourth Bern Conference on cooperation among multilateral environmental agreements with a view to enhancing the implementation of the Framework by multilateral environmental agreements, based on the findings of the global report and global review and to providing options to better align planning, monitoring and reporting obligations under the Convention and those under other relevant processes;"},{"t":"48. Encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations to support the reporting by indigenous peoples and local communities on the implementation of the Framework including by continuing to support community-based monitoring and information systems and initiatives such as the Local Biodiversity Outlook;"},{"t":"49. Requests the Executive Secretary:"},{"t":"(a) To take into account the present decision and the gaps, challenges, barriers and opportunities identified in the global report [and its key messages] in [the Secretariat’s future work over the period 2026–2030, including] the review of the programmes of work;"},{"t":"(b) To facilitate efforts by Parties and actors other than national Governments to share experiences, lessons learned and best practices in the implementation of the Framework, including"},{"t":"8 The section of paragraph 41 related to the Global Environment Facility will be duplicated in the decision on the financial"},{"t":"mechanism to be adopted at the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"10/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件 – 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件 – 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"監測架構與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之執行；8]","html":"<p>監測架構與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之執行；8]</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"41. **邀請**國家政府以外之行為者、技術與科學合作支援中心、生物多樣性相關公約及其他相關多邊環境協議之秘書處、聯合國實體及政府間組織，支持締約方改善國家監測與知識管理系統之努力；","html":"<p>41. <strong>邀請</strong>國家政府以外之行為者、技術與科學合作支援中心、生物多樣性相關公約及其他相關多邊環境協議之秘書處、聯合國實體及政府間組織，支持締約方改善國家監測與知識管理系統之努力；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"42. **鼓勵**締約方充分利用現有機制、工具、技術與科學合作支援中心、能力建構與發展倡議及計畫，以及強化區域合作，以強化監測與知識管理系統；","html":"<p>42. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方充分利用現有機制、工具、技術與科學合作支援中心、能力建構與發展倡議及計畫，以及強化區域合作，以強化監測與知識管理系統；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"43. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、國家政府以外之行為者，以及支持綱要執行之技術與科學合作支援中心，在履行其各自職責且在相關之職權範圍內時，利用全球報告、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中所包含之資訊；","html":"<p>43. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、國家政府以外之行為者，以及支持綱要執行之技術與科學合作支援中心，在履行其各自職責且在相關之職權範圍內時，利用全球報告、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標及國家報告中所包含之資訊；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"44. **鼓勵**締約方與國家政府以外之行為者分享執行綱要之經驗、經驗教訓與最佳實務，包括將其上傳至資訊交換機制之虛擬圖書館，並**邀請**締約方在相關情況下利用該等資訊；","html":"<p>44. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方與國家政府以外之行為者分享執行綱要之經驗、經驗教訓與最佳實務，包括將其上傳至資訊交換機制之虛擬圖書館，並<strong>邀請</strong>締約方在相關情況下利用該等資訊；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"[45. **邀請**締約方參與關於全球審查與加速執行綱要之葉里溫路徑（Yerevan Pathway）之區域與次區域對話[[，與決議 15/6 第 20 段一致][，旨在適當地分享行動與努力][並在適當情況下分享[任何][其]各自之行動與努力；]]]","html":"<p>[45. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方參與關於全球審查與加速執行綱要之葉里溫路徑（Yerevan Pathway）之區域與次區域對話[[，與決議 15/6 第 20 段一致][，旨在適當地分享行動與努力][並在適當情況下分享[任何][其]各自之行動與努力；]]]</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[45. 替代方案\n**邀請**締約方參與旨在加速執行綱要之區域與次區域對話；]","html":"<p>[45. 替代方案<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>締約方參與旨在加速執行綱要之區域與次區域對話；]</p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"46. **邀請**相關夥伴組織，特別是技術與科學合作支援中心，與秘書處協調，在適當情況下基於現有程序，針對第一次全球審查之結果舉辦工作坊或對話，以促進同儕學習並分享經驗與最佳實務；","html":"<p>46. <strong>邀請</strong>相關夥伴組織，特別是技術與科學合作支援中心，與秘書處協調，在適當情況下基於現有程序，針對第一次全球審查之結果舉辦工作坊或對話，以促進同儕學習並分享經驗與最佳實務；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"47. **邀請**聯合國環境規劃署舉辦第四屆伯恩會議，以促進多邊環境協議之間之合作，旨在根據全球報告與全球審查之結果，透過多邊環境協議強化綱要之執行，並提供選項以使公約下之規劃、監測與報告義務，與其他相關程序下之義務能更佳地接軌；","html":"<p>47. <strong>邀請</strong>聯合國環境規劃署舉辦第四屆伯恩會議，以促進多邊環境協議之間之合作，旨在根據全球報告與全球審查之結果，透過多邊環境協議強化綱要之執行，並提供選項以使公約下之規劃、監測與報告義務，與其他相關程序下之義務能更佳地接軌；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"48. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府及相關組織，支持原住民族與地方社區就綱要執行情況進行報告，包括持續支持以社區為基礎的監測與資訊系統及倡議，例如地方生物多樣性展望（Local Biodiversity Outlook）；","html":"<p>48. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府及相關組織，支持原住民族與地方社區就綱要執行情況進行報告，包括持續支持以社區為基礎的監測與資訊系統及倡議，例如地方生物多樣性展望（Local Biodiversity Outlook）；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"49. **請求**執行秘書：","html":"<p>49. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書：</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(a) 考慮本決議，以及在全球報告中識別出之差距、挑戰、障礙與機會[及其關鍵訊息]，於[秘書處 2026–2030 年期間之未來工作，包括]對工作計畫之審查；","html":"<p>(a) 考慮本決議，以及在全球報告中識別出之差距、挑戰、障礙與機會[及其關鍵訊息]，於[秘書處 2026–2030 年期間之未來工作，包括]對工作計畫之審查；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"(b) 促進締約方與國家政府以外之行為者分享執行綱要之經驗、經驗教訓與最佳實務之努力，包括","html":"<p>(b) 促進締約方與國家政府以外之行為者分享執行綱要之經驗、經驗教訓與最佳實務之努力，包括</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"---\n8 第 41 段與全球環境基金相關之部分，將在第十七次締約方大會將採納之關於財務機制之決議中重複出現。","html":"<hr />\n<p>8 第 41 段與全球環境基金相關之部分，將在第十七次締約方大會將採納之關於財務機制之決議中重複出現。</p>","en":[15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6adb11ba6c2d1463a4b038ff/p011.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 9 (a) – version 3 – 23 October 2026"},{"t":"on actions taken in follow-up to the global review, including through the virtual library of the clearing-house mechanism, while promoting North-South, South-South and triangular cooperation;"},{"t":"(c) To provide a summary of the information submitted pursuant to subparagraph 49 (b) above at a meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation held before the eighteenth meeting of the conference of the Parties, subject to the availability of resources;"},{"t":"(d) To continue to coordinate with partner organizations, including the technical and scientific cooperation support centres, the facilitation of peer-to-peer learning and capacity-building activities[, subject to the availability of resources];"},{"t":"[(e) To facilitate, in coordination with Parties, the technical and scientific cooperation support centres and relevant stakeholders, the holding of subregional and regional dialogues on the global review and the Yerevan Pathway for accelerating the implementation of the Framework and to compile views from Parties and stakeholders for the preparation of such dialogues, subject to the availability of resources;]"},{"t":"(f) To make the information contained in the submitted national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national targets, national reports and commitments from actors other than national Governments more easily accessible;"},{"t":"(g) To make the findings from the global report easily accessible, including through the development of information dashboards on the clearing-house mechanism of the Convention on Biological Diversity;9"},{"t":"(h) To continue to coordinate and collaborate with relevant partners to provide capacitybuilding and development support to Parties and actors other than national Governments aimed at improving national monitoring and knowledge management systems."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"9 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"11/11"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 9 (a) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 3 版 – 2026 年 10 月 23 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"透過資訊交換機制之虛擬圖書館等方式，針對全球審查後所採取之行動，同時促進南北合作、南南合作及三角合作；","html":"<p>透過資訊交換機制之虛擬圖書館等方式，針對全球審查後所採取之行動，同時促進南北合作、南南合作及三角合作；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"(c) 在第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之執行附屬機構會議上，在資源可取得之情況下，針對依據上述第 49 (b) 小項所提交之資訊提供摘要；","html":"<p>(c) 在第十八次締約方大會召開前召開之執行附屬機構會議上，在資源可取得之情況下，針對依據上述第 49 (b) 小項所提交之資訊提供摘要；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(d) 繼續與夥伴組織（包括技術與科學合作支援中心）協調，促進同儕學習與能力建構活動[, 在資源可取得之情況下]；","html":"<p>(d) 繼續與夥伴組織（包括技術與科學合作支援中心）協調，促進同儕學習與能力建構活動[, 在資源可取得之情況下]；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"[(e) 與締約方、技術與科學合作支援中心及相關利害關係人協調，促進針對全球審查及「葉里溫路徑」（Yerevan Pathway）以加速落實綱要所舉行之次區域與區域對話，並在資源可取得之情況下，彙整締約方與利害關係人之意見，以利籌備此類對話；]","html":"<p>[(e) 與締約方、技術與科學合作支援中心及相關利害關係人協調，促進針對全球審查及「葉里溫路徑」（Yerevan Pathway）以加速落實綱要所舉行之次區域與區域對話，並在資源可取得之情況下，彙整締約方與利害關係人之意見，以利籌備此類對話；]</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(f) 提高提交之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標、國家報告，以及國家政府以外之行為者所承諾內容之取得便利性；","html":"<p>(f) 提高提交之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標、國家報告，以及國家政府以外之行為者所承諾內容之取得便利性；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(g) 提高全球報告研究結果之取得便利性，包括透過開發生物多樣性公約資訊交換機制之資訊儀表板；9","html":"<p>(g) 提高全球報告研究結果之取得便利性，包括透過開發生物多樣性公約資訊交換機制之資訊儀表板；9</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(h) 繼續與相關夥伴協調與合作，為締約方及國家政府以外之行為者提供能力建構與發展支援，旨在改善國家監測與知識管理系統。","html":"<p>(h) 繼續與相關夥伴協調與合作，為締約方及國家政府以外之行為者提供能力建構與發展支援，旨在改善國家監測與知識管理系統。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"__________","html":"<hr />","en":[7]},{"md":"9 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.","html":"<p>9 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.</p>","en":[8,9,10]}]}]};
